+# Full independent review request
+
+Read SOURCE_GATE.md, the original OWR contribution printed862 and BLN published Conjecture1, RESULT.md, and all five TURN_n.md files. Bind the verdict to FINAL_AUTHOR_MANIFEST.json and the final WIP receipt supplied separately. Original proposed disposition: unsolved5/5.
+
+Primary sources are locally in sources/ and bound by SOURCE_MANIFEST.json. OWR official source https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46893 ; BLN published https://proceedings.mlr.press/v134/bubeck21a/bubeck21a.pdf . The source gate records further primary URLs, the Wu–Huang–Zhang attribution correction, report2021/publication2022 dates, and the actual sphere/Gaussian norm distinction. Raw PDFs and the source-page PNG are local-only, not public packet files. The Shmalo2026 preprint is contextual, not a required theorem.
+
+Highest-risk obligations:
+- T1 root circular spacings at a random sample, not a deterministic origin; all-functions McShane optimum, exact flip-edge parity distribution, CDF endpoints and probability quantifiers.
+- T2 Poisson coupling direction, lower/upper chart density, image diameter and dimension-dependent thresholds. Gaussian claim is global/domain-appropriate, not sphere-restricted.
+- T3 empirical covariance event must hold for every adaptive projection; actual sphere-fiber lift, paired good-point counts, rank0 and high-rank cases, fixed-accuracy constants.
+- T4 full row rank must really realize every strict ReLU pattern, including the zero pattern; derive global norm from sphere homogeneity rather than assume it. Audit the centered increment moment proof, independent-copy symmetrization, conditional labels, infinite chaining/separability, and high-probability constants. The result excludes hidden biases, affine skips and dependent rows.
+- T5 sphere Lipschitz constant is spectral spread, not raw operator norm; separate even/odd parts, trace-zero balanced subset, conditional matrix/vector concentration, rank split and arbitrary output biases. Verify the fixed globally Lipschitz activation construction only realizes the quadratic-core subclass.
+- Original full target must remain unresolved. Finite checks do not replace infinite probabilistic proofs. No novelty claim or general Gaussian sphere-norm repair is made.
+
+Run python REPLAY_ALL.py from this directory; standard-library only, no raw sources required for the public algebra replay. Optional --sources sources verifies the exact local source hashes. All five stdout receipts must reproduce byte-for-byte and all historical manifest bindings must verify. The final manifest binds every public file except itself; the final remote receipt is supplied separately, avoiding a self-reference. Do not change frozen files; required corrections should be additive and explicitly reviewed.
